WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.267
-Lea Thompson!

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.033
"Some Kind of Wonderful,"
weirdly enough,

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.033
that song not in the movie,
right?

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:08.868
-Yes! It was not in the movie
of "Some Kind of Wonderful."

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:11.234
-That's pretty interesting.
-Which is the weirdest thing.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:12.567
I was like, "What?

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.601
You spent the money
for the title."

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:16.501
-Why is that song
not in the movie?

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:18.300
-Yes, my husband directed that.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.033
-Well, yeah, I mean,
that's the --

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.100
that's the good thing
that came out of that.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.701
-33 years.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:25.100
-That's what I'm talking about.
Congrats.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.968
-Hi, honey!
-Mwah! Mwah! We love you, honey!

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.334
Thank you for playing charades
with Ralph and Jennifer.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:33.767
Have you met --
-I'm so sorry for your loss.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.868
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my -- geez.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.267
-I mean, you are the home team.
-I was home team.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:41.767
But, man, that got crazy.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:44.167
Have you met those guys before,
Ralph or Jennifer?

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.601
-Well, Jennifer played
my daughter Zoey's mother

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:47.968
in "Before I Fall."
-That's right.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.234
-And I remember seeing
"Flashdance" when I did

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:51.801
"All the Right Moves,"
with Tom Cruise.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.067
That was a long time ago.
And I was a dancer.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.734
I was like, "You can dance
and weld at the same time?"

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.334
-Yeah! Of course!
-Oh, my God!

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.167
-You can do whatever you want.
-Yes.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:02.767
And, Ralph,
I auditioned for "Karate Kid,"

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.701
and I didn't get the part.
-Aww.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.701
-I was bitter until now, but
since I beat him at Charades...

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.601
I'm over it now.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:14.334
-Can we talk about the
"Back to the Future" audition?

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.267
'Cause this is
a good story, too.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.868
"Back to the Future,"
you auditioned for --

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:20.100
and spoiler alert.
-I got it!

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.601
-Yeah, you got it.
-I got the part.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:24.334
-You pretty much know that,
yeah, you got it.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.300
-But at the same time I was --

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.634
I got this part in
"A Chorus Line," the movie.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.133
-Ooh.
-So I had to pick.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.734
And it was
the girl who couldn't sing.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.167
You know that part?
-Yes.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.801
-"See, I really can't sing.
I really couldn't sing."

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:39.367
And then, so I had to decide
whether I wanted to say that

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.734
or, "Oh, my God.
It's Calvin Klein.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.200
What a dream."
-Yes!

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.868
I mean...
Choices, choices.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.434
-The choice was clear.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:50.501
-The choice
was very, very clear.

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:51.934
-So I took "Back to the Future."

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.300
But the people
from "Chorus Line"

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.701
were very upset with me.

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:59.000
And they said, "Don't you want
to be a piece of history?"

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.634
[ Laughter ]
And I guess I am.

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:03.367
-Yeah, you are, actually!
Yeah, exactly.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:07.567
Lea Thompson is a part of
history, pretty much.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.300
Also, you know what's
another part of history?

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.767
Is that you were in the very
first Marvel movie.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.834
You were in "Howard the Duck."
-Oh, yes.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.467
-I mean, this is -- that's
the very first Marvel movie.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.634
-Yes, I am
the first Marvel queen.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:20.434
-Yes!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.434
-They kind of try to keep it
on the down low

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.968
over there at Marvel Studios.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.734
No, they kind of always
hint around sneaking

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:30.434
Howard the Duck somehow back.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:32.334
I would love -- I think
we should bring it back.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.501
I think we should do it.
-See, I want --

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:38.667
I want -- I've been in to pitch
a "Howard the Duck" movie

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:42.000
with Chip Zdarsky,
who did the comic book --

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.033
the last run of the
"Howard the Duck" comic book.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.534
He put me on the cover.
And so we went in,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.367
and we pitched it.
And --

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.634
-You've been directing
for the --

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.033
I mean, you're doing --
you're crushing it.

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:53.834
I know Zoey Deutch
is your daughter, who we love,

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.133
and she's been on the show
many times.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.300
I love her.
-Yes.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.000
Absolutely one of
our favorite guests.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.934
And I always talk to her,
and she's like, "Oh, yeah,

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:03.000
my mom's directing this,
and then she's doing that."

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.701
And so I think
it would be perfect.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.267
I think, Marvel, let's do this.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.133
-I've been directing
a lot of sci-fi shows,

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.434
big shows, to learn
how to do the special effects

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.767
and all of that.
I've been doing "Star Girl."

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:15.934
I have on one that was on
tonight and one next week.

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.501
And then,
I did "Resident Alien,"

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:18.834
which is a great show.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.534
AND "Star Trek: Picard."

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.300
I took Sir Patrick Stewart
back in time.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.100
Apparently, I am an expert
at time travel.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.467
-Yeah, yeah, that's interesting.
Right?

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.767
Don't get typecast now.
-No, okay.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:34.167
But, yah, I've been trying
to learn all my special effects

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.501
just in case Marvel calls.
-Yeah.

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.167
-You guys, yeah.
-You need some more

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:40.567
women directors.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:42.767
Women.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:47.033
-Did you always want to direct?
Being such a good actor...

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.701
I mean, do you go, like,
"Ooh, I think I could be

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:49.934
on the other side"?

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.601
-Well, I'm bossy,
so there's that.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:52.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.667
-That helps,
being a bossy director, yeah.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.734
-And I've been directing
for like 17 years.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:58.934
Yeah, I kind of did,
but when you have little kids,

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.167
it's so kind of
all-encompassing.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:04.000
But I find --
I've done so many things.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.634
I was a ballet dancer, singer,
I've been on Broadway.

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:11.300
[ Coarse voice ] And I get to
use my 43 years in show biz.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.567
-Wow!
It's been forty --

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.400
-43 years.
-Let me tell you,

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.901
back in the day,
we didn't sit on couches.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.467
We sat on the floor
and talked to each other.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.200
-[ Normal voice ]
You can use all that,

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.467
like you do on this show.
You're so amazing,

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:27.701
the way you sing and you dance
and you write and you create.

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:30.634
And it's so fun to be able
to create with people

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.767
something special
that makes them laugh.

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.234
-Yeah, that's what we try to do.
-Thank you.

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:37.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.934
-We have things
we have to talk about.

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.501
We have to talk about
"The Spencer Sisters" because --

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:43.601
-Oh, okay!
-Yeah.

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.100
This is where -- you just
came from here, from set.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.834
-Yes, I just came from set.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:48.567
I'm doing "The Spencer Sisters."

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:51.834
And this is the amazing
Stacy Farber,

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:52.968
and she plays my daughter.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:55.734
I'm, like,
this fabulous mystery writer.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:58.534
I get to be like, "Oh, my God."
I've got nails and everything.

00:04:58.534 --> 00:05:00.767
And Spanx and extensions.
-Spanx.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.934
And we solve mysteries together.

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:06.167
She's an ex-cop.
-Fun.

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:09.267
-I'm in Winnipeg.
I got two jobs in Winnipeg.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:12.133
One was with Stacy Farber,
and the other

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:15.300
is "The Disappearance
of Cari Farver."

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.567
What is going on with Winnipeg
and these names?!

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:19.868
-Wait. Stacy Farber
and Cari Farver?

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.133
-Yes.
-That's bizarre.

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:22.634
-I know.
How do I remember it?

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:25.467
-Yeah. Let's talk about "The
Disappearance of Cari Farver."

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:27.534
It's on Lifetime
this Saturday, 8:00 p.m.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.300
What is the movie about?
How do we set it up?

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.467
-Well, it's just crazy.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:31.868
You know,
If one thing we've learned,

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.501
people are cray, right?
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.667
-Last five years, there's
some cray things going on.

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.667
-People are cray. It's trending
on Twitter right now.

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:39.634
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
The one thing we learned.

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:41.267
-So this is a real cray story.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:42.667
It's kind of like
a love triangle.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:45.367
A guy and two girls,
Cari and Liz.

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:49.033
And all of a sudden,
Cari disappears,

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:52.033
and she starts sending all these
horrible text messages,

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.300
and nobody knows where she is.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.067
And I play her mother.
And of course,

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:57.467
I'm the one that keeps
going to the police and saying,

00:05:57.467 --> 00:05:59.400
"Something is wrong."

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.801
-Yeah.
-There you go.

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:02.033
-That's it right there.
-That's it, in a nutshell.

00:06:02.033 --> 00:06:03.801
-You have to do it.

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:05.734
Someone has to say it.
-Someone's mom --

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:08.534
-Someone has to say,
"Something is wrong here!"

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.934 --> 00:06:11.601
"Something is wrong here!"
Yeah, there we go.

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:14.501
I auditioned for the part of
the mother. I did not get it.

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.400
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Lea Thompson in

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.868
"The Disappearance
of Cari Farver."

00:06:17.868 --> 00:06:19.634
Take a look.

00:06:19.634 --> 00:06:21.033
-Look, I know
what you're thinking,

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:24.100
but she missed
her cousin's wedding.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.767
She would never miss something
like that if she could help it.

00:06:27.767 --> 00:06:34.000
And she's taking her father to
every single chemo treatment.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.501
My daughter, Cari...

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:41.167
she is a wonderful person.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.234
She really is.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:45.367
But yesterday,
she didn't show up.

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:48.801
She didn't call,
she didn't text, nothing.

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:50.834
-Lea Thompson, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:52.834
"The Disappearance
of Cari Farver"

00:06:52.834 --> 00:06:56.267
premieres this Saturday
at 8:00 p.m. on Lifetime.

00:06:56.267 --> 00:06:58.734
We'll be right back with a
performance from Modern English!

00:06:58.734 --> 00:07:00.300
Stick around!

